=== note: what this shows
The six `loop-<timestamp>` refs are the same six before and after a whole 211-case run of this suite in this
worktree, and all six are dated 2026-10-21 / 2026-10-23 — they are the refs loop *runs* made (`tools/loop/run.sh:499`),
not the suite: a case builds a throwaway repository of its own (`tools/loop-cases.sh:549`) and the run a case starts
makes its branch and its worktree inside that one. So the interference the item suspected — two suites sharing the
ref namespace and git worktree locks of the repository they run in — does not exist in this tree, and a
per-invocation ref namespace would have changed nothing. Measured 2026-10-24, this worktree, base a0ca0f35.
